1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,278
Task Manager says Disk, 100 percent.

2
00:00:03,558 --> 00:00:05,829
Your drive isn't full, so what's maxed out?

3
00:00:06,579 --> 00:00:08,308
That number is active time.

4
00:00:08,588 --> 00:00:11,193
It's how much of the time your drive was busy.

5
00:00:11,473 --> 00:00:13,560
It says nothing about free space.

6
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:17,213
A hard drive reads one scattered spot at a time.

7
00:00:17,493 --> 00:00:22,818
Its arm swings to the right track, then waits for the platter to spin the data underneath.

8
00:00:23,098 --> 00:00:25,666
That's roughly 13 milliseconds per read.

9
00:00:26,416 --> 00:00:31,071
It manages only about 75 to 100 random reads per second.

10
00:00:31,351 --> 00:00:35,692
When startup apps all want files at once, the line never empties.

11
00:00:35,972 --> 00:00:38,875
Busy every moment means 100 percent.

12
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:41,305
An SSD has no arm.

13
00:00:41,585 --> 00:00:46,367
It answers in well under a millisecond, so the same work barely registers.

14
00:00:47,117 --> 00:00:50,968
Find the real culprit in our video, Why Your PC Is Slow.

